"For each item below, fetch its source and check that the recorded quote appears on the page and supports the item. A card item is a field of the plan in the producer's words, with the sources it cites: check each factual claim in it against those sources, and any value it carries against the page; what the plan will build, measure or predict needs no source, but a factual claim with no source is UNSUPPORTED. For a cost input, check that the page states the number for the setting given; whether it applies to this plan is not yours to judge. When the page states a different number for a num or rate item, give it as page_value. Decide only from the pages you fetch and the text below; do not read files. Return one status per item, under its ref: SUPPORTED, PARTIAL, UNSUPPORTED, CONTRADICTED or UNREACHABLE, with the page sentence you relied on.
Items, one per line:
{\"ref\":\"card:question\",\"text\":\"Does verifying more candidate coolants with GPU molecular dynamics keep raising the best figure of merit above known commercial single-phase fluids, or does it plateau?\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:hypothesis\",\"text\":\"Predictor-filtered molecular dynamics finds PFAS-free esters or hydrocarbons that beat commercial coolants [orgmol], and more candidates keep improving the best one.\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"orgmol\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41524-025-01720-4\",\"quote\":\"we apply the Org-Mol fine-tuned models to systematically screen out promising candidates for immersion coolants, which require low dielectric constant (strictly lower than 3.20 at room temperature for electrical safety), low kinematic viscosity (preferably lower than 12 cSt at 40 °C), high thermal conductivity (preferably higher than 0.140 W/m ⋅ K), and environmental friendliness.\"}]}
{\"ref\":\"card:if_lever\",\"text\":\"Best cooling figure of merit keeps climbing with candidates verified, so more compute keeps finding fluids that beat commercial ones.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:if_not\",\"text\":\"Best figure of merit plateaus by a few hundred candidates, because predictor filtering and ~10% force-field error cap how high MD-ranked fluids score.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:test_summary\",\"text\":\"Generate a million PFAS-free esters and hydrocarbons, ML-filter to a ranked shortlist, MD-verify the top 100, 300, then 1000 candidates' viscosity and thermal conductivity, and compare their cooling figure of merit to commercial fluids.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:closest_prior\",\"text\":\"Org-Mol ML-screened six million esters and experimentally validated two; it never MD-verified hundreds-to-thousands of candidates at once.\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"orgmol\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41524-025-01720-4\",\"quote\":\"we apply the Org-Mol fine-tuned models to systematically screen out promising candidates for immersion coolants, which require low dielectric constant (strictly lower than 3.20 at room temperature for electrical safety), low kinematic viscosity (preferably lower than 12 cSt at 40 °C), high thermal conductivity (preferably higher than 0.140 W/m ⋅ K), and environmental friendliness.\"}]}
{\"ref\":\"card:left_open\",\"text\":\"No study measures whether the best MD-ranked coolant keeps improving as the number of MD-verified candidates grows from 100 to 10,000.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:anchor\",\"text\":\"MD pipeline reproduces n-hexadecane thermal conductivity 0.1444 W/m/K and viscosity 2.95 mPa/s near 300 K before scoring candidates.\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"berger2024\",\"url\":\"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10765-024-03383-7\",\"quote\":\"T (K) λ (mW·m−1·K−1) Cyclohexane n-Decane n-Hexadecane Squalane ... 298.15 144.43\"}],\"value\":\"0.1444 W/m/K and 2.9523 mPa/s (n-hexadecane, ~300 K)\"}
{\"ref\":\"card:limits\",\"text\":\"Result is a ranking and hit rate, not absolute fluid accuracy; one fluid class, no mixtures, no synthesis or lifetime testing.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"src:orgmol\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41524-025-01720-4\",\"quote\":\"we apply the Org-Mol fine-tuned models to systematically screen out promising candidates for immersion coolants, which require low dielectric constant (strictly lower than 3.20 at room temperature for electrical safety), low kinematic viscosity (preferably lower than 12 cSt at 40 °C), high thermal conductivity (preferably higher than 0.140 W/m ⋅ K), and environmental friendliness.\",\"supports\":\"property thresholds diel_hi, kvisc_hi, kcond_lo; the predictor-first design; filter yield (461 monoesters pass all filters)\"}
{\"ref\":\"src:berger2024\",\"url\":\"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10765-024-03383-7\",\"quote\":\"T (K) λ (mW·m−1·K−1) Cyclohexane n-Decane n-Hexadecane Squalane ... 298.15 144.43\",\"supports\":\"anchor_k_hexadecane = 0.1444 W/m/K for n-hexadecane at 298.15 K (144.43 mW/m/K)\"}
{\"ref\":\"num:throughput_ns_day\",\"name\":\"MD throughput on one A6000 for a ~20-30k-atom organic liquid\",\"value\":500,\"unit\":\"ns/day\",\"basis\":\"PROXY\",\"quote\":\"| [ns/day] | System 1 | System 2 | System 3 | System 4 | System 5 | System 6 | ... A100 | 267.5 | 691.7 | 265.8 | 129.1 | 38.8 | 23.2 | ... A40 | 277.0 | 731.8 | 268.1 | 122.3 | 34.9 | 19.0 |\",\"page_setting\":\"GROMACS 2024.1 benchmark on NHR@FAU Alex cluster; System 1 = R-143a in hexane (20,248 atoms, very high output), System 2 = short RNA in water (31,889 atoms)\",\"differs_in\":[\"my systems are 10-45k-atom pure ester/hydrocarbon liquids with rare output, not RNA or hexane benchmarks\",\"System 1's very high output rate cuts speed ~2.6x\",\"A6000 is the same GA102 chip as the A40 (277.0 ns/day), clocked slightly differently\",\"I discount System 2's 691.7 to 500 ns/day for margin\"],\"url\":\"https://hpc.fau.de/2024/08/13/gromacs-2024-1-on-brand-new-gpgpus/\"}
{\"ref\":\"num:a6000_usd_h\",\"name\":\"Lambda on-demand A6000 price per GPU-hour\",\"value\":1.09,\"unit\":\"USD/GPU-hour\",\"basis\":\"CITED\",\"quote\":\"1x GPU tab: NVIDIA A6000 | VRAM/GPU: 48 GB | vCPUs: 14 | RAM: 100 GiB | STORAGE: 512 GiB SSD | PRICE/GPU/HR*: $1.09\",\"url\":\"https://lambda.ai/pricing\"}

